  "step_2": "The individual reviewed the amounts and probabilities of both lotteries. They explicitly stated that they chose the lottery with a 100% winning chance. The individual did not mention evaluating the expected values, comparing outcomes, or discussing the 2500 Euro possibility in A. The justification centers solely on the 100% probability of receiving money, indicating a focus on certainty and probability of a favorable outcome. There is no mention of risk, expected value, or any comparison of the monetary amounts beyond the probability of receiving something at all. The deliberation process is summarized as a simple comparison of the probability of winning (100% vs. 99%), and the individual chose the one with the highest probability of a favorable outcome.",
  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — specifically, the probability of a favorable outcome — is present in the verbal report. Lottery B has a 100% probability of a favorable outcome (2400 Euros), while Lottery A has only a 99% chance (33% + 66%). The individual explicitly chose the lottery with 100% probability, which aligns with the rule of the decision reason: preferring the lottery with higher probability of a favorable outcome. The justification in the report directly reflects this reasoning, even if it is stated simply. Thus, the individual used the decision reason to make the choice.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
